# Battle Movement Implementation

## Movement Mechanics
### Pathfinding Priority
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Target-Acquisition#Path-Calculation
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Core-Requirements#Movement-Efficiency

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Movement-Feedback#Path-Indicators
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Retargeting-Logic#Target-Acquisition

1. Follow network connection lines between nodes
2. Calculate optimal path to target using network topology
3. Identify required node stops for direction changes
4. Stop at attack range edge or closer to target

### Attack Range Behavior
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Combat-Range#Range-Calculation
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Battalion-Stats
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#State-Updates#Position-Tracking

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Attack-Positioning#Range-Updates
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Feedback#Range-Indicators
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Capture-Process#Range-Requirements

- Move until attack range edge reaches target center
- If new target already within range (or closer):
  - No movement needed
  - Begin attacking immediately
- Resume movement only if target moves out of range or is captured (node) or destroyed (battalion) 

### Position Calculation
